From e1dfb86983e36f4788d2b9505d611c4e5e0acf1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:24:39 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Mods' code patches: the functions they write into keep their
 registers in the context, and the co-op Mods tab's switches

Longshot v3.0.0's register locals (nx2/guest_locals.py, a64_lift.localize_regs)
write a function's locals back before a call and at a return except x9-x15,
which the usual calling convention leaves dead there. A mod's code need not
follow it: Character Select's routines take values in x11 and x14 and answer
in x12, so with x11 in a local of the game's function its hook sits in
(f_80c35c30, a ran_funcs.txt function) the routine read a stale x11 and the
game crashed at a pick (snaildev99, kit 0.11.6). Every function holding a
word a mod's ExeFS patch writes (the hook sites, which lift the hook's code
as their own, and the routines in the cave) now joins Lifter.no_local
(exefs_patches.functions_written, from nx2/lift.py). The patches' hash is
in the lift's key already (patch 0034), so a changed patch lifts again.

The co-op kit's Mods tab keeps its switches and order in
<mods>/coop-mods.list (patch 0011), not mods.json: with that file the
patches follow it (an off mod's patches stay out; the list's first row
wins, as host/mods.c indexes it). host/mods.c's log line no longer says
the patches are left out.
---
 host/mods.c          |  7 ++--
 nx2/exefs_patches.py | 76 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 nx2/lift.py          |  5 +++
 3 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

